    "answer": {
      "short": "$P(t)=\\dfrac{1200}{1+5e^{-kt}}$, where $k=\\dfrac12\\ln\\dfrac52$. Thus $P(5)\\approx797$ rabbits.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{dt}{dP}&=\\frac{1200}{kP(1200-P)}\\\\\n\\frac{dt}{dP}&=\\frac1k\\left(\\frac1P+\\frac1{1200-P}\\right)\\\\\nt&=\\frac1k\\left(\\ln|P|-\\ln|1200-P|\\right)+D\\\\\n\\ln\\left|\\frac{P}{1200-P}\\right|&=kt-kD\\\\\n\\frac{P}{1200-P}&=Ae^{kt}\n\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $P(0)=200$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{200}{1000}&=A\\\\\nA&=\\frac15\\\\\n5P&=(1200-P)e^{kt}\\\\\nP(5+e^{kt})&=1200e^{kt}\\\\\nP(t)&=\\frac{1200}{1+5e^{-kt}}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $P(2)=400$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\n400&=\\frac{1200}{1+5e^{-2k}}\\\\\n1+5e^{-2k}&=3\\\\\ne^{-2k}&=\\frac25\\\\\nk&=-\\frac12\\ln\\frac25\\\\\nk&=\\frac12\\ln\\frac52\\approx0.4581.\n\\end{align*}$$\nHence\n$$\\begin{align*}\ne^{-5k}&=\\left(\\frac25\\right)^{5/2}\\\\\nP(5)&=\\frac{1200}{1+5(2/5)^{5/2}}\\\\\nP(5)&\\approx797\\text{ rabbits}.\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
